- "The Original Work": the Work in its original form as distributed by the Licensor.
- "Derivative Work": a work based upon the Work, in particular a work created by modifying, adapting or translating the Work.
- "The Source Code": the human-readable form of the Work which is the most convenient form for a person to study and modify the Work.
- "The Object Code": any form of the Work other than the Source Code.
- "The Licensor": any natural or legal person who offers the Work under the terms of the Licence.
- "You": any natural or legal person who uses, modifies or distributes the Work under the terms of the Licence.
- "Distribution": any act of distributing, communicating, making available to the public or placing on the market the Work or copies thereof.

